1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Change one rule. Watch the world respond.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
A rising tide changes what is land and what is water.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:23,000
At high tide, the trail loses its dry connection.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
As the tide retreats, the reef and route emerge again.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
A height field shows a surface. A density field describes a volume.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Subtract a tunnel to make space beneath the surface.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Reverse the operation order. The pillar survives.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
A local edit rebuilds nearby chunks, not the whole volume.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
One branching rule starts with five segments.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Three grammar iterations produce 125 segments.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Leaf clusters turn the branching structure into a tree.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Now time advances: individuals grow, seed and compete.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Population is a history of births and deaths, not just a density slider.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Observe. Change a rule. Discover what follows.
